1. ADD WTXID / WITNESS-VARIANT MODEL
====================================

This is blocking.

Qogecoin Core distinguishes:

  txid = GetHash()
       = serialization hash WITHOUT witness

  hash = GetWitnessHash()
       = full serialization hash INCLUDING witness
       = wtxid

See Core TxToUniv:

  "txid" -> GetHash()
  "hash" -> GetWitnessHash()

Therefore different valid witness serializations can share the same txid
while having different wtxids.

The current schema cannot preserve that:

- transactions is keyed only by txid
- size/vsize/weight live on transactions
- block_transactions references only txid
- transaction_input_witness is keyed only by txid/vin/item

That means two competing blocks containing the same txid but different
witnesses cannot both be represented faithfully.

Correct this before schema freeze.


PREFERRED MODEL
---------------

Keep:

  transactions

as the immutable NON-WITNESS transaction identity/body:

  txid PRIMARY KEY
  version
  locktime
  is_coinbase
  fee_satoshis
  indexed_at

Inputs and outputs remain keyed by txid because they are part of the txid
serialization.

Move witness-dependent metrics out of transactions:

  size
  vsize
  weight

Add a new table, e.g.:

  transaction_variants

with:

  wtxid TEXT PRIMARY KEY
  txid TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES transactions(txid)
  size INT NOT NULL
  vsize INT NOT NULL
  weight INT NOT NULL
  indexed_at ...

and:

  UNIQUE (wtxid, txid)

For a transaction without witness:

  wtxid == txid

which is fine — it still has one variant row.


BLOCK OCCURRENCES
-----------------

block_transactions must identify the actual serialization that appeared
in that block.

Store both:

  txid
  wtxid

and enforce:

  FOREIGN KEY (wtxid, txid)
    REFERENCES transaction_variants(wtxid, txid)

Keep:

  PRIMARY KEY (block_hash, tx_index)

and the existing useful:

  UNIQUE (block_hash, txid)

if it is consistent with Core-valid chain history.


WITNESS STORAGE
---------------

transaction_input_witness must be variant-specific.

Do NOT key witness data solely by txid.

Use something equivalent to:

  wtxid
  txid
  vin_index
  item_index
  data BYTEA

with:

  PRIMARY KEY (wtxid, vin_index, item_index)

  FOREIGN KEY (wtxid, txid)
    REFERENCES transaction_variants(wtxid, txid)

  FOREIGN KEY (txid, vin_index)
    REFERENCES transaction_inputs(txid, vin_index)

This guarantees witness item N belongs both to:
- the correct full transaction serialization
- an actual vin of the underlying txid transaction body.


